'''ESO 410-G005''' is a dwarf spheroid galaxy. It is a member of the [[Sculptor Group|Sculptor galaxy group]] but is relatively isolated. It has a low surface brightness.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last1=Karachentsev |first1=Igor D. |last2=Sharina |first2=Margarita E. |last3=Grebel |first3=Eva K. |last4=Dolphin |first4=Andrew E. |last5=Geisler |first5=Doug |last6=Guhathakurta |first6=Puragra |last7=Hodge |first7=Paul W. |last8=Karachentseva |first8=Valentina E. |last9=Sarajedini |first9=Ata |last10=Seitzer |first10=Patrick |date=October 2000 |title=Hubble Space Telescope Photometry of the Dwarf Spheroidal Galaxy ESO 410-G005 |url=https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2000ApJ...542..128K/abstract |journal=The Astrophysical Journal |language=en |volume=542 |issue=1 |pages=128–136 |doi=10.1086/309514 |bibcode=2000ApJ...542..128K |issn=0004-637X|arxiv=astro-ph/0007001 }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.aanda.org/articles/aa/full/2002/22/aa2298/node2.html |access-date=1 August 2025 |website=www.aanda.org|title=Photometry of southern field dwarfs}}</ref>

The galaxy has a stellar population with intermediate age population.<ref name=":0" />

